    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">1867 Compromise</a> turned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> lands into a Dual Monarchy: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#hungary">Hungary</a> under one ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#franz-joseph-i">Franz Joseph</a>.</li><li>Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#vienna">Vienna</a> produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sigmund-freud">Freud</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#gustav-mahler">Mahler</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#gustav-klimt">Klimt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ludwig-wittgenstein">Wittgenstein</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#bohemia">Bohemia</a> became a major industrial region.</li><li>The war it began in 1914 broke its multinational army, and it dissolved into successor states in October 1918.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#budapest">Budapest</a> was only created in 1873, by uniting Buda, Óbuda and Pest, and grew to almost 900,000 people by 1910.</p></aside>
    </section>

